HST Office on macOS: no declaration that clashes with an installed LibreOffice.

- Info.plist: the ODF, OpenOffice.org and extension types are imported, not exported (LibreOffice
  exports them; two exports of one type conflict); their document types are LSHandlerRank Default
  instead of Owner, so installing HST does not take the default application from LibreOffice
  (HST stays under Open With, and is the default where no owner is installed); LibreOffice's URL
  schemes vnd.libreoffice.cmis/command and vnd.sun.star.webdav(s) are dropped (the Microsoft
  Office ms-* schemes stay); CFBundleSignature is ???? instead of LibreOffice's LibO.
- Spotlight importer: own bundle id vn.hasontech.hstoffice.mdimporter and CFPlugIn factory UUID
  instead of LibreOffice's org.libreoffice.mdimporter / A3FCC88D-..., so both importers stay
  registered. The Quick Look extensions already derive their ids from the bundle id.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).

